TITLE='Authentic title "Why Everything Changes After You Hit $500,000 Invested" promises a threshold explanation. The script delivers the crossover-point idea, fee and behaviour-gap warnings, and options (Coast FIRE, geographic arbitrage, products), with a candid reality check that $500K is not rich. The "everything changes" promise rests on expected, not guaranteed, returns.'
THUMB='Registered maxresdefault 1280x720 (HTTP 200, real image). White background: a heavier-set cartoon man in a white shirt pointing at an open safe stacked with green banknotes, with "THE $500K RULE" in heavy black capitals ($500K largest) and a curved arrow pointing at the safe. At 320x180 the text reads clearly. Mild mismatch: the script describes a milestone, not a named "rule".'
SCRIPT='A single-narrator story-driven explainer with composite Alan (and George as foil): hook on Alan at $48K, crossover point at 8-10%, median-income comparison, Munger quote, milestone timeline, doubling time, 1% fee drag, concentration risk, Alan at $512K, Coast FIRE, geographic arbitrage, product access, lifestyle creep, Morningstar and Dalbar behaviour gaps, Barber and Odean, boredom gambling, reality check (4% rule, tax on traditional accounts, SCF rarity), Alan vs George at 60, close. Most headline arithmetic reproduces; the milestone timeline does not, the Alan path is internally inconsistent and future crashes are narrated as past events.'
